    {
      "id": "II-infra-recovery-group2-01FB-proofparagraph",
      "statement_id": "cdp:st:C.3.5",
      "tag": "01FB",
      "source_sha256": "33e5e01d81b96aed7be0d5af71fc4425537f534af855b5f50d7b3a4b0835c573",
      "before": "\\begin{proof}\n\\begin{enumerate}[label={$\\langle1\\rangle$\\arabic*.},leftmargin=*]\n\\item \n\\noindent\\textbf{Step 1.} All the listed smooth surfaces have Euler number zero by \\ref{cdp:st:C.3.1}.\nAdditivity of compactly supported Euler characteristic for the\nstratification by the smooth-fibre locus and the finitely many\nexceptional fibres gives\n$e(Y)=e_c(C\\setminus\\Delta)e(F)+\\sum_{c\\in\\Delta}e(Y_c)$.\nThe first term vanishes. A scheme-theoretic fibre and its reduction\nhave the same underlying topological space, so their topological\nEuler numbers agree. Chern--Gauss--Bonnet gives the first equality.\n\n\\end{enumerate}\n\\end{proof}",
      "after": "\\begin{proof}\nAll the listed smooth surfaces have Euler number zero by \\ref{cdp:st:C.3.1}.\nAdditivity of compactly supported Euler characteristic for the\nstratification by the smooth-fibre locus and the finitely many\nexceptional fibres gives\n$e(Y)=e_c(C\\setminus\\Delta)e(F)+\\sum_{c\\in\\Delta}e(Y_c)$.\nThe first term vanishes. A scheme-theoretic fibre and its reduction\nhave the same underlying topological space, so their topological\nEuler numbers agree. Chern--Gauss--Bonnet gives the first equality.\n\n\\end{proof}",
      "type": "D03/D08",
      "reason": "Remove the repeated Step 1 and iteration/list wrapper from the single proof paragraph; all substantive math and references remain.",
      "comparison_record": "agents/ii_infra/recovery_20261121/S6_SERIES_PUBLISH_II_second_group_comparison.json",
